.TH AGENT-INSTALL 1 "2026-10-29" "agent-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agent-install \- print the command that installs a coding agent
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agent-install
.BR claude | codex | agy
[\fIversion\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B agent-install
prints a command that downloads a coding agent's native installer from its
vendor and runs it, for you to read and then run with
.BR "agent-install ... | sh" .
It runs nothing itself.
.PP
The installer is run so that it leaves shell startup files such as
.I ~/.bashrc
alone, and with
.I ~/.local/bin
on its
.BR PATH ,
where all three install. Add that directory to your
.B PATH
yourself if it isn't already.
.TP
.B claude
Claude Code, from
.IR https://claude.ai/install.sh .
It only suggests the
.B PATH
line, which
.I ~/.local/bin
on its
.B PATH
silences.
.I version
is
.BR stable ,
.B latest
or a version number.
.TP
.B codex
Codex, from
.IR https://chatgpt.com/codex/install.sh .
It appends a
.B PATH
block to
.I ~/.bashrc
or
.I ~/.zshrc
unless its bin dir is on
.B PATH
and no other
.B codex
is found, so it runs with a throwaway
.B HOME
from
.BR mktemp (1)
and with
.B CODEX_INSTALL_DIR
and
.B CODEX_HOME
set to the real
.I ~/.local/bin
and
.B $CODEX_HOME
or
.IR ~/.codex .
.B CODEX_NON_INTERACTIVE
keeps it from offering to start Codex or uninstall another one.
.I version
is
.B latest
or a version number.
.TP
.B agy
Antigravity CLI, Google's successor to Gemini CLI, from
.IR https://antigravity.google/cli/install.sh .
It only suggests the
.B PATH
line. It installs only the latest version, and does nothing if
.I ~/.local/bin/agy
exists: agy updates itself.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR agent\-ps (1),
.BR claude\-user (1)
